# API conventions

Resource-based endpoint naming. Planned MVP paths:

| Method | Path |
|---|---|
| GET | `/health`, `/health/db` |
| POST | `/auth/login` |
| GET | `/users/me` |
| POST | `/jd/parse` |
| POST | `/gaps/compute` |
| GET/POST | `/applications` |
| PATCH/PUT/DELETE | `/applications/{id}` |
| GET/POST | `/notes` |
| DELETE | `/notes/{id}` |
| POST | `/quiz/generate` |
| POST | `/quiz/submit` |
| POST | `/interview-prep/generate` |
| GET | `/interview-prep/{jd_id}` |

Keep this style for new routes. Contract details: `docs/api.md` (update when routes ship).

## Auth

Every **authenticated** endpoint requires a Supabase session token (`Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`) and **verifies `user_id` server-side** before querying. Never trust client-supplied `user_id`. Health routes stay public.

## Errors

Always return structured JSON, never raw stack traces:

```json
{ "error": "message" }
```

## Frontend

All frontend API calls go through a **single shared client** (`frontend/lib/api.ts`) instead of scattered `fetch()` calls. That client attaches the session token, uses the API base URL from env, and surfaces `{ "error": "message" }` consistently.
